## Errors & Mistakes
- In the first version of this commit, no test covered the null path
  of prefill capacity_classes, so a regression for the default
  configuration would have passed. Removing the attribute resolved it.
- The first version of TestDeploymentPDLifecycle had a same-config
  plan-only step and state checks that repeat what terraform-plugin-
  testing and Terraform core already check after every apply step.
  They were removed.

## Attempts & Outcomes
- Applied update steps in the mock lifecycle wait for
  rolloutStartGracePeriod (30 s) each. The change and removal steps are
  therefore plan-only with a PostApplyPreRefresh plan check, the pattern
  from #456.
- An earlier prototype was +395 lines with an example and more tests.
  The first version of this commit was +256/-1; this one is +210/-1.
- The second review pass proposed moving TestDeploymentPDLifecycle into
  deployment_hotload_test.go to save the 15-line package clause and
  import block. This was refuted: every test file in
  coreweave/inference is named for the tests it holds, #456 gave
  hot_load its own deployment_hotload_test.go, and #458 kept a small
  test in its own file next to the file that defines its fake.

## Findings & Constraints
- The pinned buf.build/gen/go/coreweave/inference module
  (v1.36.12-20261008185853-22f8f31f8962.2) already has DeploymentPD, so
  no dependency bump is needed. It has no autoscaling claims field.
- terraform-plugin-testing v1.16.0 runs a non-refresh plan and a
  refresh plan after every apply step and fails when either is not
  empty. It rejects PreApply plan checks on a PlanOnly step;
  PostApplyPreRefresh runs on that step's plan.
- The API message cannot tell an empty repeated list from an unset
  one. This is why a list attribute needs the prior model value to keep
  a configured empty list.

